course: dictionary
lesson: 2991
title: Dull: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which meaning to use. «Dull» is a good example. Read the sentence first, then ask which meaning fits.
explain: «The old door knob was dull, not shiny.» The clue is shiny, so dull means not bright. «The lesson was dull, so Leo nearly fell asleep.» Now the clue is lesson, so dull means boring. Same word, different meaning.
explain: «Dull» can also describe a sound or a pain. «She had a dull ache in her back» means a steady, heavy pain, not a sharp one. When a word could mean two things, try each meaning in the sentence and keep the one that makes sense.
fact: «Dull» can be an adjective or a verb. To dull something is to make it less strong or less bright.
fact: «Dull» can mean boring: «But isn't it a bit dull at times?» asks the Mole.
fact: «Dull» can mean not bright or shiny: the thin dull layer on a brass door knob is rubbed off, and the metal stays bright.
fact: «Dull» can mean not sharp: a dull pencil or blade needs sharpening.
fact: Phrases to remember: «a dull day», «a dull ache», «dull the pain», «never a dull moment».
exercise: «The old door knob was dull, not shiny.» What does dull mean here? | Sharp | *Not bright | Exciting | Very loud
exercise: «Whenever Alice asks a sensible question, the creatures call her dull.» What does dull mean here? | Clever and quick | Loud and cheerful | Shiny and bright | *Boring and uninteresting
exercise: «She had a dull ache in her back.» What kind of pain is it? | *A steady, heavy pain that is not sharp | A sharp, sudden pain | A very bright pain | A loud pain
test: «The sky was dull and grey all day.» What does dull mean here? | Sharp and pointy | Sunny and bright | Loud and noisy | *Cloudy and grey
test: To «dull the pain» means what? | *To make the pain less strong | To make the pain shiny | To make the pain sharp | To make the pain louder
exam: «The pencil is dull, so Ella sharpens it.» What does dull mean here? | Exciting and fun | *Not sharp | Very long | Bright and shiny
